bank_freeze_notice.template:
OFFICE OF THE INVESTIGATING OFFICER, POLICE STATION: {{policeStation}}, UTTAR PRADESH POLICE

To:
The Nodal Officer / Branch Manager
{{bankName}}, Branch: {{branchName}}

SUBJECT: Notice under Section 94 and Section 107 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), 2023 for URGENT DEBIT FREEZE and account statements in FIR No. {{firNo}}.

Sir/Madam,

1. It is brought to your urgent attention that FIR No. {{firNo}} dated {{firDate}} has been registered at PS {{policeStation}} under Section 318(4) BNS 2023 and Section 66D IT Act regarding cyber financial fraud involving misappropriation of Rs. {{defraudedAmount}}/-.

2. During active cyber investigation and money trail tracing via 1930/CFCFRMS portal, the following account maintained with your bank has been identified as a direct recipient/mule account holding proceeds of crime:
   - Beneficiary Account Name: {{accountHolder}}
   - Account Number: {{accountNumber}}
   - IFSC Code: {{ifscCode}}
   - Disputed Transaction UTR / Ref No: {{transactionRef}}
   - Transferred Amount: Rs. {{transferredAmount}}/-
   - Date & Time of Transfer: {{transferDateTime}}

3. In exercise of powers conferred under Section 107 BNSS 2023, you are hereby ORDERED TO PLACE AN IMMEDIATE TOTAL DEBIT FREEZE on the above-mentioned account to prevent siphoning of proceeds of crime.

4. Under Section 94 BNSS 2023, you are required to furnish the following within 24 hours of receipt of this notice:
   (a) Certified Account Ledger statement from {{statementFromDate}} to date with Section 63 BSA certificate.
   (b) Account Opening Form (AOF), KYC documents (Aadhaar, PAN, Photo, Mobile Number).
   (c) IP logs, device details, and ATM withdrawal CCTV footage if any.

Failure to comply shall attract penal action under Section 223 BNS (Disobedience to order duly promulgated by public servant).

Investigating Officer:
Rank: {{ioRank}}
Name: {{ioName}}
P.NO: {{ioPno}}
Police Station: {{policeStation}}
District: {{district}}, Uttar Pradesh

